web-digest Repository Version History
=====================================

v1.1.0 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Added an opt-in "Summarize in Japanese" setting; off by default, the summary keeps
  using the page's own language as before.
- Added a choice of AI provider: Sakura AI Engine, OpenAI or Claude, selected in
  settings; one run uses exactly one selected provider. Sakura AI Engine remains the
  default, and an existing Sakura user's token, model and Japanese summary preference
  keep working with no migration and no change on their part.
- Added independent credential and model storage per provider (openaiApiKey,
  openaiModel, anthropicApiKey, anthropicModel), alongside the existing apiToken and
  model keys, which stay Sakura's own. Switching providers never touches another
  provider's stored credential or model.
- Added OpenAI support through its native Responses API (store:false, no tools, no
  streaming) and Claude support through Anthropic's native Messages API (no
  compatibility layer, no tools, no streaming); Sakura's own Chat Completions request
  is unchanged.
- Added optional host permissions for api.openai.com and api.anthropic.com, requested
  only when the reader selects that provider in settings, or, for whichever of the two
  is currently selected, from a "Grant or restore permission" action there; Sakura's
  host permission stays required. A denied selection request leaves the previous
  provider selected; a permission later revoked in Chrome fails the next run before the
  page is read, and can be restored from that action without changing the selected
  provider. No fallback to another provider in either case.
- Renamed the error kinds and reader-facing messages to be provider-neutral (for
  example token-missing to credential-missing, engine-error to provider-error), since
  a run may now use any of the three providers.

v1.0.1 (2026-08-26)
-------------------
- Aligned the supported Chrome version with what opening the side panel actually requires.
- Stopped work that finishes after its tab was closed from restoring the removed session state.
- Prevented summaries from starting when their side panel could not be opened.

